WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.062 --> 00:00:04.089
"Please gather some eggs," Chef said.

2
00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:07.432
He handed baskets to everyone.

3
00:00:07.433 --> 00:00:10.651
"We're making French toast today."

4
00:00:10.652 --> 00:00:13.972
"Yes!" Bobby cried.

5
00:00:13.973 --> 00:00:16.642
"I'm wearing my lucky shirt.

6
00:00:16.643 --> 00:00:21.109
Whenever I wear it, something good happens.

7
00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:28.194
Once I hit a home run with it!"

8
00:00:28.195 --> 00:00:33.757
Nina put three eggs in her basket. "Thanks, chickens!"

9
00:00:33.758 --> 00:00:37.015
Bobby reached down to grab an egg.

10
00:00:37.016 --> 00:00:39.694
He heard a loud rip.

11
00:00:39.695 --> 00:00:45.312
"Oh, no! I just tore my good luck shirt."

12
00:00:45.313 --> 00:00:49.640
"That's bad luck," Jason said.

13
00:00:49.641 --> 00:00:54.408
"Bobby, your shirt is too small for you," Izzie said.

14
00:00:54.409 --> 00:00:57.295
"No wonder it ripped."

15
00:00:57.296 --> 00:01:04.336
Bobby shrugged. "I bet my mom can sew it."

16
00:01:04.337 --> 00:01:08.191
The kids carried the eggs into the kitchen.

17
00:01:08.192 --> 00:01:11.522
Everyone looked at the recipe.

18
00:01:11.523 --> 00:01:16.365
"We need four eggs for French toast," Izzie said.

19
00:01:16.366 --> 00:01:21.356
"Remember to crack them properly!" Chef said.

20
00:01:21.357 --> 00:01:25.765
Each kid cracked an egg into a shallow dish.

21
00:01:25.766 --> 00:01:31.011
Jason added milk. Then Bobby whisked the mixture.

22
00:01:31.012 --> 00:01:37.342
"Chef, does French toast come from France?" Nina asked.

23
00:01:37.343 --> 00:01:42.881
"No, people first made this dish in ancient Rome," Chef said.

24
00:01:42.882 --> 00:01:46.875
"I heard that a man named French made it popular in America.

25
00:01:46.876 --> 00:01:49.212
But I'm not sure it's true.

26
00:01:49.213 --> 00:01:53.344
Today people all over the world eat fried egg bread."

27
00:01:53.345 --> 00:01:59.834
Bobby grinned. "I want lots of maple syrup on mine!"

28
00:01:59.835 --> 00:02:04.413
"We'll try different toppings today," Chef said.

29
00:02:04.414 --> 00:02:07.656
"Like what?" Jason asked.

30
00:02:07.657 --> 00:02:11.387
Chef pointed to some ingredients on the counter.

31
00:02:11.388 --> 00:02:16.278
Bobby saw ketchup, cheese, peanut butter, and yogurt.

32
00:02:16.279 --> 00:02:19.092
"Ugh," Bobby thought.

33
00:02:19.093 --> 00:02:23.071
"This isn't my lucky day after all."

34
00:02:23.072 --> 00:02:26.410
He didn't want any of those toppings.

35
00:02:26.411 --> 00:02:30.408
Chef melted butter in a frying pan.

36
00:02:30.409 --> 00:02:34.132
"Now let's dip a slice of bread in the egg mixture.

37
00:02:34.133 --> 00:02:39.231
We're using stale bread because it soaks up the egg nicely."

38
00:02:39.232 --> 00:02:42.806
Izzie dipped a slice of bread in the egg mixture.

39
00:02:42.807 --> 00:02:46.313
She turned it over.

40
00:02:46.314 --> 00:02:49.328
"There! I coated both sides.

41
00:02:49.329 --> 00:02:53.023
It's ready for the frying pan!"

42
00:02:53.024 --> 00:02:57.777
The other kids each took a turn dipping bread slices.

43
00:02:57.778 --> 00:03:02.086
Soon four slices were frying in the pan.

44
00:03:02.087 --> 00:03:07.421
After a few minutes, Chef lifted the corner of each bread slice.

45
00:03:07.422 --> 00:03:12.236
"They're golden brown. Let's flip them over."

46
00:03:12.237 --> 00:03:15.006
"I'll do it," Jason said.

47
00:03:15.007 --> 00:03:18.372
"I'll help," Nina said.

48
00:03:18.373 --> 00:03:25.305
When the French toast was ready, Chef put it on plates.

49
00:03:25.306 --> 00:03:28.644
"Now choose your topping."

50
00:03:28.645 --> 00:03:37.769
Izzie spread yogurt on her slice. "Yum!"

51
00:03:37.770 --> 00:03:42.812
"I'm going to try mine with cheese," Nina said.

52
00:03:42.813 --> 00:03:48.173
"Ketchup sounds weird, but I'll try it," Jason said.

53
00:03:48.174 --> 00:03:52.391
"That's how they eat it in England," Chef said.

54
00:03:52.392 --> 00:03:54.826
Bobby crossed his arms.

55
00:03:54.827 --> 00:03:58.539
"I only like French toast with syrup."

56
00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:00.970
Chef lifted an eyebrow.

57
00:04:00.971 --> 00:04:04.908
"Part of cooking is trying new dishes."

58
00:04:04.909 --> 00:04:08.180
Bobby frowned, watching his friends eat.

59
00:04:08.181 --> 00:04:11.548
"I like things to stay the same."

60
00:04:11.549 --> 00:04:14.771
Finally he couldn't stand it anymore.

61
00:04:14.772 --> 00:04:18.038
"I'll try peanut butter."

62
00:04:18.039 --> 00:04:22.556
"Great," Chef said.

63
00:04:22.557 --> 00:04:26.379
The warm bread melted the peanut butter.

64
00:04:26.380 --> 00:04:31.895
Bobby took a taste. "It's pretty good!"

65
00:04:31.896 --> 00:04:38.643
Chef smiled. "See, change can be good."

66
00:04:38.644 --> 00:04:42.395
Later the kids walked outside together.

67
00:04:42.396 --> 00:04:47.140
"My lucky shirt really is too small," Bobby said.

68
00:04:47.141 --> 00:04:49.692
"Time for a new one."

69
00:04:49.693 --> 00:04:54.015
"Just don't spill peanut butter on it!" Jason said.

70
00:04:54.016 --> 00:05:02.372
Bobby laughed. "That would be unlucky for sure!"

